      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T09:28:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Like I noted in the high-level reply, I think it would make more sense to have another BackingObject, or even maybe create a new type of BackingObject (e.g., RestrictedBackingObject?), and have that as a second backing object in MemoryRegion.\n\nThis is mainly to support use-cases where there are two backing objects for the same memory (one for shared and one for private). I also think that it might make the plumbing a bit simpler.",
      "revId": "1a52951c0c11be0c810e181b70a0282506f8dab6",
